<title>INDIA: India to float 16-bln-rupee state gvt loans Jan 20.</title>
<headline>India to float 16-bln-rupee state gvt loans Jan 20.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>India said on Wednesday it would float the third tranche of state government loans for 1996/97 (April-March) on January 20.</p>
<p>The loans would be for an aggregate amount of 16.09 billion rupees, the Finance Ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The loans will be of 10-year maturity and carry a coupon rate of 13.75 percent per annum,&quot; it said.  </p>
<p>The statement said all 25 state governments would enter the market.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11-301 2024</p>
